  "audience": {
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "programmeDescription": "Sociology at Erasmus University Rotterdam examines social change through theory, qualitative and quantitative research, and work with professional organisations. Its curriculum addresses inequality, population and family life, culture and identity, cities and migration, cohesion and conflict, and planetary change.",
    "comparisonExplanation": "Three UCR programmes combine sociological theory and research with other fields: broad social inquiry; politics, rights and inequality; or society, sustainability and technology. They offer meaningful related study, while the dedicated population/family and urban/migration sequence and the required 15-EC internship and 15-EC bachelor project remain gaps.",
